.TH RUSTKET 1 "2026-11-08" "rustket @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustket \- native Rocket.Chat desktop client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustket
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fILINK\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustket
is a Rocket.Chat client that renders everything natively instead of embedding a
web browser. Browser sign-in (OAuth, OpenID, SAML, CAS) and video calls use the
default browser and return through \fBrocketchat://\fR links.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user: links given on the command line (for example
\fBrocketchat://auth?...\fR or a server URL) are forwarded to the running
instance, which opens them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ICED_BACKEND=tiny\-skia
Use the CPU renderer instead of the GPU (the same as turning hardware
acceleration off in the settings).
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example \fBRUST_LOG=debug\fR. Logs are written to standard error.
.TP
.B RUST_BACKTRACE=1
Print a backtrace when the application crashes; include it in bug reports.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustket/config.toml
Servers and preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/rustket/
Image and message cache; safe to delete while the application is not running.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustket/
Fallback token store (\fBsecrets.json\fR, mode 0600), used only when no Secret
Service keyring is available. Tokens are normally kept in the keyring.
